docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1091:- `poc/concurrency_study/runner.py`: opt-in callable day runner, bounded extraction lookahead, request validation, immutable worker inputs, manifest and cleanup. Invoked through `replay.run(day_runner=...)`; default remains serial. The POC uses a single coordinator/writer and does not claim support for other processes writing this ledger.
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1095:- `jev_matching.decide(workers=1)`: plan independent questions on the coordinator, send only immutable state/questions to threads, collect answers and mutate candidates/totals in original order. The default remains serial. A refused answer fails the item; successful concurrent responses remain archived for retry.
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1099:- Persistent POC manifest: ordered input identities and source digests, sequence numbers, configuration, universe and code/prompt digests per day. Resume must match. A changed source/configuration is refused before speculative submission. Interrupted manifest creation refuses with a clear error rather than guessing.
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1107:| Before day | Same manifest on resume | Reuse; default dispatch retains original sequences |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1108:| Before day | Changed/corrupt manifest | Refuse before launching calls; no source or ledger rewrite |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1117:| Matching | One question fails | Drain remaining calls; fail the item without a write; resume can reuse completed archived requests |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1120:| Restart | Saved accepted handover exists | Use normal resume; do not speculatively re-extract it |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1134:| Per-day manifest | POC coordinator → restart | Exact source/configuration/order match; no silent config or source replacement |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1136:| Failure/retry | Existing round and replay | No later authoritative progress; completed prefix reused on restart |
docs/research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review.log:1138:Tests use real temporary databases and real stored source material where available; only model/provider responses are faked. Cases: independent overlap; schema-only invalidation; same-day new thesis; changed group membership; failed earlier call; out-of-order completion; accepted-handover resume; writer failure; no later-day work; Jev response ordering and partial failure/cache reuse; manifest mismatch. Positive controls and scratch mutants must fail for stale-answer acceptance and completion-order mutation. The default sequential tests remain unchanged.
